Check that the public reporting channel is published, that the product documentation tells customers how to report security issues, and that the internal channel is published. Also check that people are named to monitor the shared channels and to route the reports, and that each report from a shared channel has been given to a team.

{{#if this.craGuidance}}
== EU Cyber Resilience Act

The CRA (Regulation (EU) 2024/2847) requires that the manufacturer of a product with digital elements:

* puts in place and enforces a policy on coordinated vulnerability disclosure (Annex I, Part II, point 5)
* makes it easier to share information about potential vulnerabilities, and gives a contact address for reporting vulnerabilities (Annex I, Part II, point 6)
* designates a single point of contact, so that users can communicate with the manufacturer directly and rapidly, also to report vulnerabilities (Article 13(17)).

Give the contact address and the single point of contact in the user information of each product.
